 "_note": "Width scan at FIXED depth (6 layers), FIXED learning rate (1.0e-3) and FIXED batch (2M tokens), across d_model 128/256/512 -- a 4x width and 16x non-embedding-parameter range. Verified against the EleutherAI model card before running, because 14m and 31m were added after the initial Pythia release. The card also states all models saw the exact same data in the exact same order, so a timing difference here cannot be data order, learning rate, or depth. This is the confound C20 could not break: there, LR falls as size rises and the crossing order tracks the LR order exactly, tie included. A null is publishable and was pre-registered as such. lambda statistics exclude unignited runs (F42) with n stated; rank tests keep every run. The 70m cells duplicate dev_transition_scale.json by design and are re-run rather than imported, turning the redundancy into a determinism check across independent invocations."
}